Design a CGOA binding for a C API that creates and frees a Book object and returns its title. Given C:
typedef struct Book Book;
Book* create_book(const char* title);
const char* book_title(Book*);
void free_book(Book*);
Implement a CGO Go wrapper exposing:

 type BookHandle struct { ptr *C.Book }

func NewBook(title string) (*BookHandle, error)
func (b *BookHandle) Title() (string, error)
func (b *BookHandle) Close() error

Ensure ownership is explicit (Close frees) or a finalizer, no leaks, and demonstrate two concurrent book creations and title fetches?

